{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "note": "F4-014, closed. Shared oracle for the executor's decision logic — token binding, spend-before-effect ordering, EXECUTE's permanent refusal, and the whole-workspace coverage requirement. Both rust/crates/noesar-executor and services/reference-control-plane/src/executor.mjs must satisfy every case, each building the same scenario natively (real files, a real TokenMinter with the same 32-byte secret [7,7,...], a real shadow) because execute() has real side effects and is not a pure function the way shadow's compare() is — only the setup and the expected shape of the outcome are expressible as data. 'plan: other' means the token is minted against a second authorized plan (same step id, files = bench.files plus one extra path) so its digest differs from the plan actually being executed against. D-0253: EXEC-011/012 extend this oracle to the two zero-process decision branches D-0250 added on the JS side and this phase mirrors on the Rust side (EXECUTE mechanically present but disabled-by-operator; enabled but the token carries no isolation envelope). Neither spawns a real process, so both remain portable vectors like the ten before them — the class of vector that DOES spawn a real noesar-sandbox process is deliberately NOT here (D-0250's own reasoning: a vector only one side could satisfy would be worse than none), and instead lives as native, binary-presence-gated tests on each side (services/reference-control-plane/test/sandbox-runner.test.mjs on the JS side; rust/crates/noesar-executor/tests/sandbox_live.rs on the Rust side, added by D-0253).",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "EXEC-001",
      "why": "a valid token authorises the action; only the shadow changes, never the source",
      "bench": {
        "files": {
          "a.txt": "before"
        },
        "destructive": false
      },
      "mints": [
        {
          "paths": [
            "a.txt"
          ],
          "operations": [
            "WRITE"
          ],
          "uses": 1,
          "plan": "self"
        }
      ],
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "WRITE",
          "path": "a.txt",
          "contents": "after"
        }
      ],
      "expectation": {
        "pathsTheDiffMustTouch": [
          "a.txt"
        ]
      },
      "expected": {
        "performed": 1,
        "refused": 0,
        "ok": true,
        "shadowFiles": {
          "a.txt": "after"
        },
        "sourceFiles": {
          "a.txt": "before"
        }
      }
    },
